%I A398723 #19 Sep 10 2026 22:33:30
%S A398723 0,4,6,8,11,18,28,32,43,53,63,76,88,102,119,134,151,170,188,210,230,
%T A398723 251,276,299,325
%N A398723 Maximum population of a Conway still life in an n X n square whose live cells are connected by king moves.
%C A398723 Two live cells are adjacent when they share an edge or a corner; all live cells must belong to one component under this adjacency (a chess king can traverse through the entire construction). Births immediately outside the square are forbidden.
%C A398723 Further proved values are a(31) = 497, a(32) = 528, a(33) = 562, and a(39) = 782. The first unresolved term satisfies 349 <= a(26) <= 352.
%C A398723 Each exact result has both a connected stable witness and a matching upper proof. The linked repository indexes the proof route and evidence for every claimed exact value.
%C A398723 The problem appears as the Connected Maximum-density Still Life benchmark of the Fourth Answer Set Programming Competition in 2013. It was used as one of the problems in the verifiable track for CAISc 2026.
%H A398723 ASP Competition 2013, <a href="https://www.mat.unical.it/aspcomp2013/ConnectedMaximumDensityStillLife">Connected Maximum-density Still Life</a>.
%H A398723 G. Chu and P. J. Stuckey, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.artint.2012.02.001">A complete solution to the Maximum Density Still Life Problem</a>, Artificial Intelligence, 184-185 (2012), 1-16.
%H A398723 Conference For AI Scientists (CAISc) 2026, <a href="https://caisc2026.github.io/verifiable-problems/?problem=connected-still-life">Connected Still Life, Verifiable Problems Track</a>.
%H A398723 Siddhartha Mahajan, <a href="https://github.com/Siddhartha-Mahajan/connected-still-life/tree/v1.0.1">Maximum connected still lifes: witnesses, bounds, and reproducible optimality proofs</a>.
%H A398723 Siddhartha Mahajan, <a href="/A398723/a398723.svg">Illustrations of the proved optima for n = 1..25</a>
%F A398723 For n >= 14, a(n) <= floor((4*n^2 + 5*n - d(n mod 8))/8), where (d(0),...,d(7)) = (26,23,18,23,20,23,26,11).
%F A398723 a(n) <= A055397(n), the unrestricted still-life maximum.
%e A398723 a(2) = 4, realized by the 2 X 2 block.
%Y A398723 Cf. A055397.
%K A398723 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A398723 1,2
%A A398723 _Siddhartha Mahajan_, Sep 05 2026
